    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d597">

                <pb facs="0715" n="617" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg617"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2613: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-13T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 14—2:20
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>12. Your December 20, 4 p.m.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d597-f1"/> and Legation’s
                    December 31, noon.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d597-f2"/> Unless the Pacific
                    Development Corporation acts upon its loan option, the influence of Williams in
                    reorganization of wine and tobacco bureau will probably be insufficient to
                    accomplish the <pb facs="0716" n="618" xml:id="pg618"/> desired result. It
                    trust[s] that the Department will consider carefully its attitude toward the
                    loan and send me instructions as soon as possible in order to relieve the
                    Legation from an embarrassing situation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d597-f1" n="65" xml:id="d597-f1-content">
                <p><ref target="frus1919v01#pg_548"><hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>, p.
                    548</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d597-f2" n="66" xml:id="d597-f2-content">
                <p>Reporting: “[C. L. L.] Williams now definitely appointed Co-Director General of
                    the Wine and Tobacco Administration from December 1st.” (File no.
                    893.51/2598.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
